bonsai-oryon (0.3.0) experimental; urgency=low

  * CPU backend modules now use ggml's own threadpool instead of OpenMP; the
    OpenMP-threaded modules of v0.2 are kept in /usr/lib/bonsai-oryon/omp.
  * 0007: BONSAI_PROFILE=1 graph profiler; bounded spin-then-yield barrier
    (BONSAI_BARRIER_SPIN).
  * 0008: --oryon-profile balanced|throughput|low-power|auto|none (default
    auto for cli/server, reads the profile written by bonsai-tune).
  * 0009: opt-in barrier-free single-token matmul (BONSAI_TG_NOBARRIER=1).
  * New /usr/bin/bonsai-tune; rewritten bonsai-benchmark.sh (interleaved
    randomized rounds, condition tracking, confidence intervals); helper to
    run older release .debs without installing them.

 -- SatoruGoj0 <SatoruGoj0@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000

bonsai-oryon (0.2.0) experimental; urgency=low

  * 0005: 4-row interleaved PQ2_0 layout (CPU_REPACK) for single-token decoding.
  * 0006: opt-in lossless ternary 4-row layout (BONSAI_PQ2_TERNARY=1, 1.75 bpw).
  * Add /usr/lib/bonsai-oryon/bin/bonsai-diag; extended benchmark script.

 -- SatoruGoj0 <SatoruGoj0@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

bonsai-oryon (0.1.0) experimental; urgency=low

  * Initial release: PrismML llama.cpp e3de715 + Bonsai-Oryon patches 0001-0004.
  * NEON PQ2_0 x Q8_K kernel (de-interleaved decode, bsums offset folding, 2x2 tile).
  * NEON quantize_row_q8_K, bit-identical to the reference.
  * armv8.6_nosve CPU variant so Snapdragon X (I8MM, no SVE) gets I8MM kernels.
  * Backends load only from /usr/lib/bonsai-oryon.

 -- SatoruGoj0 <SatoruGoj0@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
